course: dictionary
lesson: 4040
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word gel can be a thing you touch or a way of becoming something. When you meet it, look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Hand gel with alcohol kills many germs, but not all» is about a thick, sticky substance you rub on your skin.
explain: The same word can also describe what happens to a group of people. If a team starts to work well together, it has begun to gel. You can check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
explain: Lots of words in English are like this. Think of run: you can run a race, run a bath, or run out of time. Each meaning needs different clues from the sentence. Good readers stop and ask, «Which meaning fits here?»
fact: Gel is a thick, wobbly or sticky substance, between a liquid and a solid.
fact: Examples of gel are «hair gel», «hand gel», «shower gel» and «ice gel pack».
fact: To gel means to become firmer, like jelly setting.
fact: When people gel, they start to work well together, like a team that is getting better.
fact: Alcohol hand gel kills many germs, but soap and water is better when hands are dirty.
exercise: «Hand gel with alcohol kills many germs, but not all.» What is hand gel? | A kind of football boot | A type of cloud that brings rain | *A thick, sticky substance you rub on your hands | A game played in the playground
exercise: After practice, the players started to gel as a team. What does gel mean here? | To melt into water | To be paid for playing | *To start to work well together | To wash their hair
exercise: Which of these is used to style hair? | *Hair gel | Ice gel pack | Shower gel | Hand gel
test: The jelly will gel in the fridge. What does gel mean here? | *To become firmer, like jelly setting | To wash in warm water | To melt and run away | To fly up high
test: Why is soap and water better after the toilet? | Because soap is flammable | Because gel is a solid | Because hand gel kills all germs | *Because hand gel does not remove dirt
exam: Which sentence uses gel to mean a thick, sticky substance? | The players started to gel after practice | *Rub a little hand gel into your palms | The cake began to gel in the tin | Our team will gel by spring
